site: contract the footer, and drop the pages it used to carry

One pass, one kind of cut: a page or a block that restated something the site already says
somewhere better.

The footer is now the address block and the legal line.

- No page list. The header menu is the whole menu.
- No channels. The hero leads with them and `/meet/` carries the full list from `community.yml`.
- `nav.yml` `footer` becomes `elsewhere`, which renders nowhere: `page` prints no `<h1>`, so it is
  the only way the header can still name the page you are on.

Two pages dropped.

- `/about/`, which handed its board and governance material to `/meet/` already. The history it
  held a place for lands there too; `org.mission` renders on the homepage.
- `/contact/`, and the 22 links at it become `mailto:` on `org.email`. All 22 already meant
  "email us". On a phone the station pages now open a composed email, not a page load.
  `/connect` goes to `/meet/`.

Merge qualifications:
- [x] `bundle exec jekyll build` clean
- [x] Playwright `--grep-invert @external`: 535 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed
- [x] secrets, internal-publish and token guards pass
- [x] no internal link 404s; every Wix `from` still resolves
- [x] the header still names the `elsewhere` pages

Carried, not decided:
- Facebook was only in `org.yml` `social`, which nothing renders now, so it is on no page.
  `community.yml` `channels` is the live list and does not carry it. OPEN.md says so.
- `/nonprofits/` and `/policies/non-discrimination/` are linked from nothing and still in the
  sitemap — the honest state of a page nobody has decided to carry.
- 22 prompts to email us across the station pages is too many. Autumn's next pass; the number is
  the problem, not the target.

